<article class="env-definition" id="03X8">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03X8">Definition <span data-tag="03X8">59.20.1</span>.</a> (See Topologies, Definitions <a href="/tag/021M" data-tag="021M">34.7.1</a>, <a href="/tag/0225" data-tag="0225">34.6.1</a>, <a href="/tag/021Z" data-tag="021Z">34.5.1</a>, <a href="/tag/0215" data-tag="0215">34.4.1</a>, and <a href="/tag/020O" data-tag="020O">34.3.1</a>.) Let $\tau \in \{ fppf, syntomic, smooth, {\acute{e}tale}, Zariski\} $. A family of morphisms of schemes $\{ f_ i : T_ i \to T\} _{i \in I}$ with fixed target is called a <em>$\tau $-covering</em> if and only if each $f_ i$ is flat of finite presentation, syntomic, smooth, étale, resp. an open immersion, and we have $\bigcup f_ i(T_ i) = T$. </p>
</article>